    {
      "n": 4,
      "title": "Confirmation bias",
      "outcome": "Look for what would prove you wrong, not only for what agrees with you.",
      "why": "Once you believe something, you look where it will be confirmed and skip where it might not. Each look feels like proof. It is the same room, searched again.",
      "reachesYou": "The feed that only shows what you already like, the friend you ask because you know their answer, the reviews you read only after you bought it.",
      "do": "Pick one thing you are sure of. Find the best case against it, written by someone who knows the subject. Read it to the end before you answer it.",
      "voices": [
        "wason",
        "nickerson"
      ],
