    {
      "n": 5,
      "title": "Anchoring",
      "outcome": "Notice when the first number you heard is setting the price, and set your own first.",
      "why": "The first number you hear becomes the ruler you measure everything after it with, even when that number was made up. Sellers say theirs first for a reason.",
      "reachesYou": "Car stickers, \"was $90\", the first offer in a raise talk, a hospital bill you negotiate down, a home's asking price.",
      "do": "Before your next big purchase or pay talk, write down what you think it is worth, from your own research, before you hear their number.",
      "voices": [
        "kahneman",
        "northcraft"
      ],
      "scene": {
