      "title": "Loss aversion",
      "outcome": "Weigh a possible loss and an equal gain on the same scale.",
      "why": "Losing something hurts about twice as much as gaining the same thing feels good. So people pass up good chances to avoid small risks, and hold on to bad ones to avoid admitting a loss.",
      "reachesYou": "Staying in a job you have outgrown, keeping a stock that keeps falling, buying the extended warranty, \"free trial\" offers that count on you hating to lose what you already have.",
